      "title": "FHIR core definitions",
      "description": "The FHIR core specification's definitions for each STABLE release, with HL7's publication as the authority (owner, 2026-11-15): one graph per release keyed by canonical URL (http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/<id>). `pins.json` pins HL7's own package for each release at the URL HL7 publishes it (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/hl7.fhir.r4.core.tgz, R4B, R5) by sha1 and sha512; a registry mirror is pinned by its own hashes and only ever fills the cache. `<release>/manifest.json` lists every resource, complex and primitive type and root type with HL7's published JSON for it (https://hl7.org/fhir/R4/patient.profile.json), its kind, base and the sha256 of its bytes in HL7's package; constraint profiles, extension definitions and logical models are left out and counted. `<release>/class-model.json` is the UML class model derived from HL7's package (`fhir-core.ts uml`), which HL7 publishes only as pictures: a class per type and backbone element, with generalization and attributes, each citing its definition and element. Local copies of the bodies are a labelled cache (`<release>/cache/`, `fhir-core.ts materialise`), never committed. `fhir-core.ts check` holds all of it to the pins, `resolve` answers with HL7's URL, and `diagram` prints a type's class diagram. A release whose package could not be read is `unread` with the reason, never an empty graph.",
      "fileCount": 0,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/fhir-harness/directory/fhir-core-definitions"
